                <pb facs="0617" n="605" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg605"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890D.01/619: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-28T20:00:00-04:00">July 28, 1942—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3515. Department’s 3484, July 25, midnight. Consul at Beirut has reported that
                    Lebanese Ministry resigned July 23, severely criticized for failure to supply
                    bread. Cabinet was weak, Foreign Minister listening exclusively to Spears while
                    President Naccache worked closely with Catroux.</p>
                <p>On July 24 President Naccache handed Gwynn for transmission to Department a
                    letter dated July 18 which he sent to Eden complaining about Spears. Complaint
                    alleges principally that Spears had interfered in internal Lebanese affairs and
                    visited religious communities to stir up trouble. Naccache expressed the hope
                    United States Government would aid in obtaining transfer of Spears.</p>
                <p>Gwynn believes General Wilson has recommended Spears’ removal but cannot state
                    this for a fact.</p>
                <p>Spears was expected to leave Beirut for Cairo July 27 and Catroux the next day,
                    and an attempt to bring them together may be made.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
